Experiment  9:  Develop  a  program  to  demonstrate  weather  station readings using Arduino



AIM:  To  design  and  implement  an  Arduino-based  weather  station  that measures and displays temperature and humidity in real time.



COMPONENTS:

Sl. No.	
Quantity	
Component
1	1	Arduino Uno R3
2	1	USB Cable
3	3	Jumper Wire
4	1	DHT22 Sensor


 
CIRCUIT CONNECTIONS:



DHT22 Pin	
Arduino
VCC(+)	5V
GND(-)	GND

Data	
Digital Pin D2




SETUP:

a) Connect the DHT22 sensor to the Arduino Uno according to the circuit: VCC to 5V, GND to GND, and Data to digital pin D2.
b) Connect the Arduino Uno to the computer using a USB cable.
c) Open the Arduino IDE, go to Tools, select Board, and choose Arduino
Uno.
d) In Tools, select Port and choose the COM port for your Arduino.
 

e) Install the DHT sensor library by Adafruit if it is not already installed. f) Type the program into the Arduino IDE and upload it to the Arduino.
g) Open the Serial Monitor to see the temperature and humidity readings from the DHT22 sensor.

CODE:

#include <DHT.h>
#define DHTPIN 2
#define DHTTYPE DHT22
DHT dht(DHTPIN, DHTTYPE);


void setup() { Serial.begin(9600); dht.begin();
Serial.println("Weather Station Initialized");
}


void loop() {
float temperature = dht.readTemperature(false);
float humidity = dht.readHumidity();


if (!isnan(temperature) && !isnan(humidity)) { Serial.print("Temperature: "); Serial.print(temperature);
Serial.print(" °C, Humidity: "); Serial.print(humidity); Serial.println("%");
} else {
Serial.println("Failed to read from DHT sensor!");
}


delay(1000);
}


RESULT:


The Arduino-based weather station using the DHT22 sensor successfully measured  and  displayed  real-time  temperature  and humidity.  The  sensor provided accurate readings, and the program correctly processed and output the data on the Serial Monitor
